5 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410898 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $M(-4,3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410898 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c09c350-e142-585c-9d61-fa93c5184487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410898 #edb/ref 1074 "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $M$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410899 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410899 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410899 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410899 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,-5,1⟩+s⟨3,-6,0⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410899 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4fcca2b7-695c-58b7-b034-c1fa748f47da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410899 #edb/ref 1074 "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨2,-5,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-6,0⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨6,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,3,3⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410900 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410900 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410900 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410900 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(-3,-2,0)$ and $V(1,0,-1)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410900 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59e1275b-72d1-5efa-8072-c2d963838f7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410900 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨-3,-2,0⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410901 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410901 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70967" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410901 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410901 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $R(\\sqrt{2},3,-1)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410901 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e3aacfb-29e6-50e7-83f4-efffd6632659" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410901 #edb/ref 1074 "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $R$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410902 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410902 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410902 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410902 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $E(2,-1,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨3,-1,5⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨6,-2,4⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d22837b0-87ad-552e-9bb4-a7dfb550ed51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410902 #edb/ref 1074 "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $E$ is $p=⟨2,-1,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨3,-1,5⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨6,-2,4⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-1,4⟩+s⟨3,-1,5⟩+t⟨6,-2,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
